{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"26670fae9f3f52c4ac2482b4b19380659eed08ac211e88d60cbf61e0a80456d4","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found two errors: stones should be lifted by 0.2, not sunk by 0.3, and the twig's kink was mistakenly scaled by stick thickness instead of length, making it far too small. I'll fix both and give the bend its own dedicated attribute.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GFGVqrjaPXR64ZSeFRyaZY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = 'js/clutter.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nrep = [\n(\"\"\"/* a twig: a six-sided stick along x (-0.5..0.5), radius 1, with a kink in the middle */\nfunction twigGeometry() {\n  const pos = [], idx = [];\n  const rings = [[-0.5, 0, 1], [0.05, 0.12, 0.85], [0.5, 0, 0.55]];      // x, bend (z), radius\n  for (const [x, bend, r] of rings) for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) {\n    const a = (k / 6) * Math.PI * 2;\n    pos.push(x, Math.sin(a) * r, bend + Math.cos(a) * r);\n  }\"\"\",\n\"\"\"/* a twig: a six-sided stick along x (-0.5..0.5), radius 1, thinning to the tip,\n   with a kink in the middle (\\\\`bend\\\\`, sideways, in lengths: it scales with the length) */\nfunction twigGeometry() {\n  const pos = [], bends = [], idx = [];\n  const rings = [[-0.5, 0, 1], [0.05, 0.08, 0.85], [0.5, 0, 0.55]];      // x, bend, radius\n  for (const [x, bend, r] of rings) for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) {\n    const a = (k / 6) * Math.PI * 2;\n    pos.push(x, Math.sin(a) * r, Math.cos(a) * r);\n    bends.push(bend);\n  }\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(pos, 3));\n  geo.setIndex(idx);\n  geo.computeVertexNormals();\n  return geo;\n}\n\nconst KINDS\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(pos, 3));\n  geo.setAttribute('bend', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(bends, 1));\n  geo.setIndex(idx);\n  geo.computeVertexNormals();\n  return geo;\n}\n\nconst KINDS\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  geo.setAttribute('normal', geometry.attributes.normal);\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  geo.setAttribute('normal', geometry.attributes.normal);\n  if (geometry.attributes.bend) geo.setAttribute('bend', geometry.attributes.bend);\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"        uniform float uN, uSpacing, uRadius, uDensity;\n        varying vec3 vTint;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"        uniform float uN, uSpacing, uRadius, uDensity;\n        ${stone ? '' : 'attribute float bend;'}\n        varying vec3 vTint;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"        vec3 lp = position * sc;\n        lp.y -= 0.3 * sc.y;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"        vec3 lp = position * sc;\n        lp.y += 0.2 * sc.y;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"        vec3 lp = position * sc;\n        lp.y += rad * 0.7;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"        vec3 lp = position * sc;\n        lp.z += bend * len * (h2.z > 0.5 ? 1.0 : -1.0);\n        lp.y += rad * 0.7;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"        // from grit to the odd fist-sized stone, each its own proportions, a third sunk\"\"\",\n\"\"\"        // from grit to the odd fist-sized stone, each its own proportions, a third sunk\n        // (the stone is 1.24 high in its own units: lifted 0.2, a third of it stays below)\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a, b in rep:\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\nnode --check js/clutter.js && grep -n \"\\\\\\\\\\`bend\" js/clutter.js","description":"Fix stone sinking and twig bend scaling"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
