visorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"29476fa7-cb9e-4478-b456-79a9f8a97316","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ALhNxH4H7yKcpa74wzPahi","type":"tool_result","content":"7:   clutter.js). The height (float, read texel by texel, \\`GROUND_GLSL\\`): the\n23:/* GLSL for the height: \\`groundY(xz)\\`, with the mesh's triangulation\n25:export const GROUND_GLSL = /* glsl */ `\n30:  float groundY(vec2 xz) {\n142:    /* the uniforms GROUND_GLSL reads */\n/* Hedgerow — the ground map: what grows and lies where.\n\n   Two textures over the terrain's grid, made once at load, read by the\n   GPU-placed ground cover. The cover (half-float RGBA, filtered): R how\n   grassy the ground is (grass.js), G how stony (the mud of lanes, yards and\n   the street's edges), B how much fallen wood (the forest floor; both\n   clutter.js). The height (float, read texel by texel, \\`GROUND_GLSL\\`): the\n   height of the ground as the terrain mesh draws it — the mesh has a vertex\n   at every grid point in its fine chunks but only every second one\n   elsewhere, so the points between are rebuilt from its triangles (a stone\n   placed on the grid's own heights there could sink centimetres under it).\n   The splat weights come from the mesh's vertices too; the points between\n   are filled from their neighbours. Slope\n   and water are judged at every point, from the heights: nothing on steep\n   banks or under the water. Nothing inside anything solid either (houses,\n   walls, sandbags; a thin post or plank clears at least the nearest points\n   to it). */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\n\nconst smoothstep = (a, b, x) => { const t = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (x - a) / (b - a))); return t * t * (3 - 2 * t); };","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bcb1dc36-2eb0-409a-9bfd-b052744acb0c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:32:19.879Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"7:   clutter.js). The height (float, read texel by texel, \\`GROUND_GLSL\\`): the\n23:/* GLSL for the height: \\`groundY(xz)\\`, with the mesh's triangulation\n25:export const GROUND_GLSL = /* glsl */ `\n30:  float groundY(vec2 xz) {\n142:    /* the uniforms GROUND_GLSL reads */\n/* Hedgerow — the ground map: what grows and lies where.\n\n   Two textures over the terrain's grid, made once at load, read by the\n   GPU-placed ground cover. The cover (half-float RGBA, filtered): R how\n   grassy the ground is (grass.js), G how stony (the mud of lanes, yards and\n   the street's edges), B how much fallen wood (the forest floor; both\n   clutter.js). The height (float, read texel by texel, \\`GROUND_GLSL\\`): the\n   height of the ground as the terrain mesh draws it — the mesh has a vertex\n   at every grid point in its fine chunks but only every second one\n   elsewhere, so the points between are rebuilt from its triangles (a stone\n   placed on the grid's own heights there could sink centimetres under it).\n   The splat weights come from the mesh's vertices too; the points between\n   are filled from their neighbours. Slope\n   and water are judged at every point, from the heights: nothing on steep\n   banks or under the water. Nothing inside anything solid either (houses,\n   walls, sandbags; a thin post or plank clears at least the nearest points\n   to it). */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\n\nconst smoothstep = (a, b, x) => { const t = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (x - a) / (b - a))); return t * t * (3 - 2 * t); };","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"056d9015-3368-4bb9-9724-c8cd28342315","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","branch":"hedgerow-grass","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"vis