{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"1c901699acc740c36152cac969fc36d06326b7c5e7afa4880c031c73e37253bc","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five tests pass. Committing the ground-detail round:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E5taBtGf4SkxkbXhAqw3xE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/config.js fun/hedgerow/js/grass.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/js/terrain.js fun/hedgerow/js/clutter.js fun/hedgerow/js/groundmap.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: stones and twigs at your feet; grass culled to the view\n\nclutter.js scatters stones in the mud of the lanes, yards and the\nstreet's muddy edges (grit to the odd fist-sized one, a third sunk, wet\nand glossy) and twigs on the forest floor (20-60 cm, bent, lying along the\nslope), within ~9 m of the camera, placed on the GPU like the grass: one\ninstanced draw per kind over camera-snapped world cells, each piece from a\nhash of its cell, some everywhere and more where noise gathers them.\nHigh and medium (quality.clutter); about 0.2-0.3 ms at 1024x768.\n\ngroundmap.js (out of grass.js) holds what grows and lies where — grass,\nstones, fallen wood — from the terrain mesh's own splat, and the ground's\nheight as the mesh draws it: outside its fine chunks the mesh has a vertex\nonly every second grid point, so the points between are rebuilt from its\ntriangles (the lane's mesh stood up to 9 cm above the grid there, burying\nsmall pieces). Stones and twigs read it exactly (float, the mesh's own\ntriangulation: 0.00 cm off over 400 samples); the grass in one filtered\nfetch with its cover.\n\nThe grass vertex shader now gives up early on tufts with no grass or out\nof view (behind the camera, off to a side, with a margin for the lean),\nwhich is most of the 42 m patch: about 1.4 ms instead of 2.6 in an open\nmeadow, 0.7 on the street.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -6","description":"Commit the stones, twigs and grass culling"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
