{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"337f1198467388f7d9b601dfcb524d4fc9e1f2127de7bdfda1ffd21bf4eb2af0","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found that the existing furrowed bark texture isn't applied to the baked tree trunks, so I'll add it via close-range projection with per-tree offsets and species-based strength (oak/pine rough, beech smooth, birch papery). First, let me check the current wet-material hook.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P9pxS8x8WVzYrAKbnGRfnS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && grep -n \"function addWeather\" js/materials.js && sed -n '/^function addWeather/,/^\\/\\* The river/p' js/materials.js | head -120 && sed -n '/const baked = new Map/,/return get((src.name/p' js/materials.js","description":"Read addWeather and the baked material resolver"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
