{"parentUuid":"469e74d4-2183-42de-8672-f7eb3c0a7e83","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFUvZyQQ4ZAKtDFxLEPq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PVGxLsDNyXipVJXTgi3D1u","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"L=\"$TMPDIR\"; for t in world-check lod-check distance-check fp-check; do node tests/$t.mjs > \"$L/$t.log\" 2>&1 && echo \"$t ok\" || { echo \"$t FAILED\"; tail -5 \"$L/$t.log\"; }; done; cd ../.. && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: bark on the trunks, close up\n\nThe baked tree textures are stretched thin over big trunks: up close a\nbeech was a smooth grey column. Within 16 m the trunks now carry the bark\ndetail texture, projected in the tree's own space from two sides of the\ntrunk and blended by which way the surface faces (so it stays on the bark\nand has no seams to speak of), shifted per tree so neighbours differ, and\nleft off what faces up or down. Strength per species: furrowed oak and\npine, smooth beech, papery birch, old dead wood; with moss low on the\ntrunk's weather side, in the furrows first. No measurable cost.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Run tests and commit the bark detail","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_read_input_tokens":645641,"output_tokens":1021,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":427,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1021,"cache_read_input_tokens":645641,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_creation":{"ephemer