{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"69e23d5c92bf7846c1d1790cce840af7f6898b7656a722c4a09696a49e48039f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found the bug: three shaders (`allied`, `axis`, `mg42_tripod`) fail to compile because my drop function references `normal` before it's declared in `main()`. I'll fix this by using the interpolated vertex normal `vNormal` instead and moving the function below the declaration, right before `main()`.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wap9JjP1E3HBw2sF8LSxmR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = 'js/materials.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nrep = [\n(\"\"\"        ${GLSL_HELPERS}\n        ${beads ? BEADS_GLSL : ''}`)\"\"\", \"\"\"        ${GLSL_HELPERS}`)\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    mat3 f = cotangentFrame(normal, -vViewPosition, uv);\"\"\", \"\"\"    mat3 f = cotangentFrame(normalize(vNormal), -vViewPosition, uv);\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"   life (a slow cycle of its own) lasts. beads(uv, weight, density, time)\n   adds the projection's drops, weighted, to beadM (how much of the pixel is\n   drop) and beadT (their tilt, in view space, from the uv's screen-space frame). */\"\"\",\n \"\"\"   life (a slow cycle of its own) lasts. beads(uv, weight, density, time)\n   adds the projection's drops, weighted, to beadM (how much of the pixel is\n   drop) and beadT (their tilt, in view space, from the uv's screen-space frame\n   round the interpolated normal: the shading normal does not exist yet when\n   the albedo is worked out). Goes just before main(), after three's varyings. */\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a, b in rep:\n    assert a in s, a[:60]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n# inject the functions before main in the fragment shader\nold = \"\"\"      .replace('#include <opaque_fragment>', `#include <opaque_fragment>\n        #ifdef OPAQUE\n          gl_FragColor.a = mirrorAlpha(roughnessFactor, mWetUp);\n        #endif`);\n    if (foliage) {\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"      .replace('#include <opaque_fragment>', `#include <opaque_fragment>\n        #ifdef OPAQUE\n          gl_FragColor.a = mirrorAlpha(roughnessFactor, mWetUp);\n        #endif`);\n    if (beads) shader.fragmentShader = shader.fragmentShader.replace('void main() {', BEADS_GLSL + '\\\\nvoid main() {');\n    if (foliage) {\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\nnode --check js/materials.js && echo parsed","description":"Move the drop functions after three's varyings"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XnRemkByLc7sKgEroXbDSe","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"REDACTED.js","content":"const G = window.hedgerow.G;\nawait stand(0.5, 112, 0.3, -0.25);\nG.renderer.render(G.scene, G.camera);\nconst progs = G.renderer.info.programs || [];\nconst bad = progs.filter(p => p.diagnostics && !p.diagnostics.runnable).map(p => ({ name: p.name, log: (p.diagnostics.fragmentShader?.log || '') + (p.diagnostics.vertexShader?.log || '') + (p.diagnostics.programLog || '') }).slice(0, 1));\nawait snap('b2_street');\nlit(true);\nawait stand(0.5, 112, 0.3, -0.25);\nawait snapCrop('b2_rifle_lit', 380, 360, 644, 408, 1);\nlit(false);\nreturn { bad: bad.map(b => ({ name: b.name, log: b.log.slice(0, 400) })) };\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NzKMekY2gJ6wPWjd6fXTNw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"REDACTED; node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/reload.js; sleep 3; node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/boot.js && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/helpers.js && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/b2.js","description":"Reload, check compile logs and capture the rifle","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Um1pef8E83ZkQC7T4sgmtZ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"REDACTED.jpg"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EnANDjUzCxqA7Y