{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"164f91443cd0917d04342072e0d6f28c39a75789ac67b36975f91b63609d7986","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found the bug: `launchNow` leaves the previous flare frozen in place instead of clearing it, which only surfaces with the manual trigger since normal play waits for the last flare to finish. I'll fix that, dial back the sky glow, and enlarge the burning point.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mpc8ivhQ3YPwoRD6o6pKjn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = 'js/flares.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nrep = [\n(\"\"\"    /* one now (checks, the menu backdrop) */\n    launchNow(cam) { f = null; launch(cam); },\"\"\",\n \"\"\"    /* one now (checks): the one burning, if any, goes out first */\n    launchNow(cam, sky = G.sky) { f = null; off(sky); launch(cam); },\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  core.scale.setScalar(4);\"\"\", \"\"\"  core.scale.setScalar(7);\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    map: glowTexture(), color: new THREE.Color(1, 1, 1).multiplyScalar(14), blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,\"\"\",\n \"\"\"    map: glowTexture(), color: new THREE.Color(1, 1, 1).multiplyScalar(10), blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a, b in rep:\n    assert a in s, a[:60]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\n\np = 'js/sky.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"  col += vec3(0.85, 0.9, 1.0) * uFlare * (pow(fl, 5.0) * (0.06 + 0.3 * cloud) + pow(fl, 90.0) * 0.5);\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"  col += vec3(0.85, 0.9, 1.0) * uFlare * (pow(fl, 8.0) * (0.04 + 0.24 * cloud) + pow(fl, 90.0) * 0.5);\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\nnode --check js/flares.js && node --check js/sky.js && echo parsed","description":"Fix launchNow, soften the sky glow, enlarge the core"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
