{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"e9106d41575c6757c1d481ca8f14bdf54db2652be6a6479801ce9394abf3d91d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Trees currently don't cast shadows since only the lamp's cube map handles shadows. I'll add a directional light along the flare's direction with an 80 m shadow map around the player (updating only while the flare burns) so tree trunks cast shadows too, while the flare's point light stays limited to haze and particles to avoid double-lighting.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WJA2bCmZokdeB9XwMuQb1z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = 'js/lights.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nrep = [\n(\"\"\"      cand.push({ x: s.x, y: s.y, z: s.z, color: s.color, intensity: flick(s), range: s.range, score: s.intensity * s.range / (1 + d2), fog: s.fog ?? 1 });\"\"\",\n \"\"\"      cand.push({ x: s.x, y: s.y, z: s.z, color: s.color, intensity: flick(s), range: s.range, score: s.intensity * s.range / (1 + d2), fog: s.fog ?? 1, noLight: !!s.noLight });\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    for (let i = 0; i < lights.length; i++) {\n      const l = lights[i];\n      const c = cand[i];\"\"\",\n \"\"\"    // the point lights: the candidates that light surfaces (a far light lit by its own means is only haze and glow)\n    let ci = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < lights.length; i++) {\n      const l = lights[i];\n      while (ci < cand.length && cand[ci].noLight) ci++;\n      const c = cand[ci++];\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a, b in rep:\n    assert a in s, a[:60]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\nnode --check js/lights.js && sed -n 118,136p js/lights.js","description":"Let far lights opt out of the point-light pool"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
